# End-to-end walkthrough for the issuer demo, runnable from Visual Studio 2022
# or VS Code (REST Client extension) — no curl/jq required.
#
# Start the app first:
#   ASPNETCORE_URLS=http://localhost:5199 dotnet run --project samples/PostQuantum.Identity.Demo
#
# Run the requests top to bottom. Named requests (`# @name`) let later
# requests reference earlier responses, so the token flows automatically.
# Note the demos rate-limit auth endpoints to 10 requests / 30 s per IP —
# rapid re-runs will (correctly) hit 429.

@base = http://localhost:5199

### Service info — confirms PQC availability and the current signing kid.
GET {{base}}/

### 1. Register — password is hashed with Argon2id (PHC string persisted).
POST {{base}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "ada", "password": "Lovelace#1843" }

### 2. Login — Argon2id verify (fail-closed), then an ML-DSA-65–signed PQ-JWT.
# @name login
POST {{base}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "ada", "password": "Lovelace#1843" }

### 3. Protected endpoint — PqJwtBearer validates signature/issuer/audience/expiry.
GET {{base}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### 4. Refresh — new token issued FIRST, then the old jti is revoked.
# @name refresh
POST {{base}}/refresh
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### 4a. The OLD token is now revoked -> expect 401.
GET {{base}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### 4b. The NEW token works -> expect 200.
GET {{base}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{refresh.response.body.$.token}}

### 5. Logout — puts the current jti on the revocation list (idempotent).
POST {{base}}/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{refresh.response.body.$.token}}

### 5a. Token after logout -> expect 401.
GET {{base}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{refresh.response.body.$.token}}

### 6. Public-key discovery — kid -> SPKI, for downstream verifiers.
GET {{base}}/.well-known/pq-jwks

### Negative: wrong password -> 401, same body as unknown user (no enumeration).
POST {{base}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "ada", "password": "wrong-password" }

### Negative: tampered token -> 401 (ML-DSA-65 signature fails, fail-closed).
GET {{base}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}tampered
